Critters is a 1986 American science fiction comedy horror film directed by Stephen
Herek in his directorial debut, and co-written with Domonic Muir.

11
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:24,000
It stars Dee Wallace, M.

12
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:42,000
Emmet Walsh, Billy "Green" Bush and Scott Grimes in his film debut.

13
00:55:54,000 --> 00:56:00,000
The plot follows a group of small, furry aliens with carnivorous behavior escaping from two
shape-shifting bounty hunters, landing in a small countryside town to feast on its inhabitants.

14
01:00:12,000 --> 01:00:18,000
Although widely believed to have been inspired by the success of Joe Dante's 1984 film Gremlins, Herek has refuted this in interviews, pointing out that the script was
written by Muir long before Gremlins went into production and subsequently underwent rewrites to reduce the apparent similarities between the two films.

15
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
The film grossed $13.2 million during its release in the United States, and spawned a Critters franchise
consisting of three sequels and a web series titled Critters: A New Binge released on Shudder.

16
01:08:48,000 --> 01:08:54,000
The fifth entry Critters Attack!

17
01:13:06,000 --> 01:13:12,000
serves as a reboot of the series.

18
01:17:24,000 --> 01:17:30,000
The film explores themes of spacecraft, small town,
sheriff, bounty hunter, sibling relationship.

19
01:21:42,000 --> 01:21:48,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark and thought_provoking.
